<https://github.com/john1hsu/aws-graph/id/amazon-s3-files> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An Amazon S3 capability, generally available since 2026-04, that exposes a general purpose S3 bucket (or prefix) as a shared NFS v4.1/4.2 file system for EC2, Lambda, ECS and EKS. Built on Amazon EFS, it caches the active working set on low-latency storage and keeps the file system and bucket synchronized in both directions, so the data never leaves S3." .
